{"nodes": [{"id": "supabase_migrations_20260909000010_transport_write_columns_transport_runs_idempotency_key", "label": "transport_runs_idempotency_key (unique index + column)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260909000010_transport_write_columns.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A run has no unique business key at all \u2014 two FOODIVA_TO_CM runs on the same date with the same vehicle type is ordinary \u2014 so R4's retry key needs its own column."}, {"id": "supabase_migrations_20260909000010_transport_write_columns_transport_lines_idempotency_key", "label": "transport_lines_idempotency_key (unique index + column)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260909000010_transport_write_columns.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The dispatch half of R4. Without it a replayed fn_dispatch_transport_line posts a second TRANSFER_OUT and a 40 kg dispatch becomes 80 kg stuck in IN_TRANSIT against a lot that can never balance. (run_id, lot_id) cannot stand in: a lot may ride one run twice when split across smoke date groups."}, {"id": "supabase_migrations_20260909000010_transport_write_columns_transport_lines_receipt_idempotency_key", "label": "transport_lines_receipt_idempotency_key (unique index + column)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/migrations/20260909000010_transport_write_columns.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A line is written twice by two different callers, so it carries two keys; sharing one would make the receipt look like a replayed dispatch. It is also what makes TC-41 deterministic \u2014 the loser of a concurrent confirm sees the key already set and raises LINE_ALREADY_RECEIVED."}], "edges": [{"source": "supabase_migrations_202609090